  "body": "Direct-PR: two-line routing update ordered by the operator (2026-11-11: \"everything Fable is now Fable 5.2; we always use the latest version\"). No issue, because it is a one-commit docs fix.\nClaim: cloud/orch\n\n**Problem.** AGENTS.md §6 and the model matrix in EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8 still name Fable 5.1.\n\n**Change.**\n- AGENTS.md §6 routes structuring work to Fable 5.2 and adds the rule \"always the latest version\". It also says how to read older version names: in a spec, issue or brief they mean the latest release; past records keep the version that ran.\n- EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §8: the tier-A row and rule 4 now name Fable 5.2.\n\n**Checked and left as they are** (records of what actually ran):\n- ADR 0013;\n- `docs/audit/*`;\n- `docs/ux/*`;\n- the \"Difficulty / model\" headers of lot specs. Those headers cover lots that are all merged, except LOT-057, which is in progress in the cloud. The new §6 sentence covers that header without editing a file a child is working on.\n\n**Tests.** Docs only. Docs consistency is the check.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGTbJ8LjeZ6VYEWrtJ)_",
