   "body": "Adversarial review round 1 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head a3e1decb\n\nThe two edited files are correct and no history record is rewritten. Two forward-looking texts still pin Fable 5.1.\n\n1. **Medium — `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md:17`.** This plan (\"Rien n'est lancé\") copies the §6 routing table under the heading \"Routage des modèles (`AGENTS.md` §6)\" and still says `Fable 5.1`. It routes work not yet done (UX-02, UX-04, the UX-11 security review).\n   - Failing scenario: a session briefed from this file runs Fable 5.1, and the file now misquotes the section it cites.\n   - Fix: change the row to `Fable 5.2`. The rest of the file names \"Fable\" without a version and needs nothing.\n2. **Low — `docs/lots/LOT-057-rest-browsing.md:4`.** The header says \"Opus 5.5 author → Fable 5.1 reviewer\" and its issue #83 is still open, so this is a live instruction, not a record.\n   - The new §6 sentence (\"a spec … that names an older version means the latest one\") covers it, but the operator asked for every Fable mention to move.\n   - Fix: change it to 5.2. The other twelve `Fable 5.1` lot headers belong to closed issues and correctly stay.\n3. **Detail — `AGENTS.md:117`.** \"Fable is Fable 5.2 since 2026-11-11\" repeats the table and will need a second edit at the next release. Optional: drop the clause.\n\nHits judged as records, correctly untouched: `docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md:128`, `docs/audit/REVIEW-fable.md:3`, `docs/audit/C-message-parsing.md:361`, `docs/ux/questionnaire/donnees.md:197`. `docs/LOTS.md`, `.github/labels.yml`, `.harness/` and `tooling/roadmap` name Fable without a version.\n\nNo contradiction with §6, §8 or EXTERNAL-AGENTS rules 1–5. Author model is Opus 5.5 (commit trailer), reviewer Fable, as §6 requires.\n\n**Verified**\n- `git diff origin/dev-swift...HEAD`: 2 files, +4/−3.\n- `git grep -n -i \"fable 5\"` plus other spellings (`fable-5`, bare \"Fable\") across the repository, each hit judged.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/fold.py --check`: ok.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py guard`: ok.\n- `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1`: 0 errors on 268 files.\n- Issue states read over REST for the eight lots whose spec pins 5.1 and that the 2026-11-02 `state.json` listed as open: only #83 is still open.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
