   "body": "Adversarial review round 2 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE** — head 0a4f5704\n\nRound 2. The three round-1 findings are fixed and the fix commit introduces nothing new.\n\n1. **Fixed (was Medium) — `docs/ux/cadrage-agents-questionnaire.md:17`.** The copied §6 table now says `Fable 5.2`, matching the section it cites.\n2. **Fixed (was Low) — `docs/lots/LOT-057-rest-browsing.md:4`.** The header of the only still-open lot that pinned 5.1 (#83) now names `Fable 5.2` as reviewer.\n3. **Fixed (was Detail) — `AGENTS.md:117`.** The sentence no longer repeats the version, so the next release changes the table only.\n\nRemaining `Fable 5.1` hits are all records of what ran and correctly stay:\n- `docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md:128`, `docs/audit/REVIEW-fable.md:3`, `docs/audit/C-message-parsing.md:361`, `docs/ux/questionnaire/donnees.md:197`;\n- twelve lot spec headers whose issues are closed (LOT-038, 052, 053, 067, 072, 080, 091, 096, 125, 130, 158, 172, 186 minus none open).\n\nThe `AGENTS.md:117` example `\"Fable 5.1\"` is intentional: it illustrates an older version named in a spec.\n\nNo contradiction with AGENTS.md §6, §8 or EXTERNAL-AGENTS rules 1–5. Author model Opus 5.5 (commit trailers), reviewer Fable, as §6 requires.\n\n**Verified**\n- `git diff a3e1decb..HEAD`: 3 files, 3 lines changed, exactly the three fixes.\n- `git diff origin/dev-swift...HEAD`: 4 files, +6/−5; `git diff --check` clean.\n- `git grep -n -i \"fable 5\"` re-run and each hit judged again.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/fold.py --check`: ok.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py guard`: ok.\n- `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1`: 0 errors on 268 files.\n- Issue states (REST) from round 1: #83 open, the other lots pinned to 5.1 closed.\n\nReviewer's own correction, sent with the verdict: the closed-lot list holds thirteen lots, not twelve. The verdict is unchanged.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
